  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is multiprofile + avgpool + weighted + imagenet_vit_l + pca_n2000 (0.635 acc, 0.618 F1, config_025). All completed experiments use pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, leaving the RNA representation choice entirely unexplored. Since RNA is the dominant modality (0.485 alone vs ~0.22 for image), the RNA encoder is a critical design decision with zero prior evidence. Question: Does a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) improve over PCA in the best-performing multimodal setup? This directly tests whether the linear PCA projection is a bottleneck or whether a nonlinear learned embedding captures biologically relevant structure that PCA misses. Why this is the best next experiment: It slots the new encoder into the already-validated best architecture (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, ViT-L), isolating the RNA encoder as the single variable changed. A clear improvement would validate the direction of learned representations and justify further exploration (e.g., scgpt); a null or negative result would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect budget toward other untested axes (e.g., transformer+weighted in config_027, or image encoder alternatives). This maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful untested design choice under the limited budget."
}

